  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ?$",
  "worked_solution": "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(0,a).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|\\frac{1}{2}|=0.5$ centered at the point $(0,0.5),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/c41b20869064a366a1b62d6189d87c540e96196891a8abe1cf9b5c240b52a881.png)",
